==Strategy==
Even though Honey Trap is unlocked after clearing [[Into the Future]] Chapter 1, don't attempt it immediately, as you will end up facing a Queen B with up to 700% stats and Kroxos up to 7000% depending on your [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]]. It's ''theoretically'' beatable without all Treasures, but it is not worth the trouble and mediocre drop reward compared to the amount of effort you will have to put in.

The boss of this Advent stage is Queen B, an Alien/Floating sniper with a huge 999 range, 12,222 damage, and, worst of all, a nasty guaranteed Slow that lasts for over 7 seconds. Combined with her moderately rapid attack speed, anything that is hit by Queen B will be permaslowed until they take damage knockbacks, and even then if they're not fast enough they'll just end up getting hit again. Queen B's main weakness as a boss, however, is her nature as a [[Long Distance]] boss. While this does allow her to pierce far past her standing range, it also results in her having an enormous blindspot where fast units can wallop damage onto her.

To counter this obvious weakness, Queen B is supported by some annoying enemies, most notably the buffed THE SLOTH, whose 32,000 damage will probably one-shot any unit you have by the time you choose to challenge this stage. Alongside peons in the form of Brollows and Kroxos, whose attacks pack quite a punch, you'll be pressed for damage without proper strategy.

To beat this stage, the quickest and most popular way to clear this stage is by solely using speedy units and chipping THE SLOTH down until it falls. This isn't too difficult since THE SLOTH's attack rate is fairly long, so your main goals for this stage will just be how well you can time and how well you can deal with waves of Brollows and Kroxos. Another method is the traditional lure strategies, where you lure Queen B to the base, stack units on her, Weaken THE SLOTH, and then obliterate THE SLOTH before he can do anything more. This is a bit more work, however, and for the average player rushing should be just fine for this stage.

==='''Key Units'''===
'''''DO NOT USE ANY UNIT WITH LESS THAN 9 SPEED IF DOING THE RUSH STRATEGY. IT WILL GET PERMASLOWED AND WASTE YOUR MONEY.'''''

*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Awakened Bahamut's insane speed and burst damage is key to beating this stage. So long as you don't time him straight into a Brollow or into an attacking SLOTH, Bahamut can get quite a number of attacks off on THE SLOTH and drastically drain its health pool.
*[[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]]/[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank]]: Your primary meatshields, as their high speed allows them to get in Queen B's blindspot very easily. Note that a Crazed Tank at level 28 is able to tank a Brollow hit.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Courier completely stomps this stage. He is too fast, has way too much damage, and way too short of a cooldown for anything in this stage to pose a threat. A level 31 Courier can tank a Brollow hit, while a level 40 Courier (or a level 36 Courier alongside a small Attack combo) can two-shot the Brollows. Alongside some small support from meatshields and other rusher options, Courier will turn this stage into rubble. While you can do this stage without Courier, the drop reward from this stage is pretty medicore, so it's best advised to just wait until you get Courier before doing this stage to spare you the extra effort.

==='''Useful Units'''===
*[[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]]: In its True Form, Catellite has Slow Immune, allowing it to easily get inside Queen B's blindspot. Its Strong vs. Alien ability allows it to tank more hits from Kroxo as well as even get a bit of chip against a Kroxo if so needed. Catellite should be your third meatshield if you need one, after the Crazed meatshields. A level 34 Catellite, or a level 31 Catellite with a Defense combo is able to tank a Brollow hit.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly Cat]]: Butterfly is not only fast but also has Massive vs. Floating, making him an incredible source of chip against Queen B. Butterfly is also good to insta-kill a Brollow or deliver chip against a Kroxo. Having Butterfly's True Form, Fishman Cat, makes him even easier to time due to his speed and damage increase.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]: Can Can Cat's huge damage per hit and cheap cost allows them to be very useful in the stage, and they are just fast enough to sneak into Queen B's blindspot to dish out devastating damage. If Talented with their '''Move Speed Up''' and '''Extra Bounties''' Talents, Can Can becomes a force of nature, easily inflitrating Queen B's blindspot, getting Double Bounty kills off on the peons, as well as being able to chip THE SLOTH at a rapid pace.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]]: If you have beaten Realm of Carnage before this stage, Maglev is a very helpful rusher here, being able to farm Double Bounty kills on the Brollows or Kroxos. You could also use it to chip THE SLOTH or Queen B, but Maglev's somewhat lengthy cooldown means that you have to use each one well.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]]: Seafarer is a bit slower compared to some of the other rushers mentioned here, but Seafarer's somewhat decent speed, Survive, and Freeze vs. Aliens can be helpful for some of the peon waves. Seafarer also doesn't have the worst damage ever, so in a pinch you can use him to get some chip against THE SLOTH.

==='''Niche Units'''===
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]: While Camera's speed makes her cumbersome to use in a rushing lineup, she can be useful in a semi-lure lineup, where her stackability and guaranteed Survive allows her to take down an incoming horde of Brollows.
*[[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Magica Cat]] and [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necromancer Cat]]: Only useful for the lure strategies, Magica is helpful to Weaken THE SLOTH to prevent your entire stack from collapsing while Necromancer Freezes Queen B alongside Seafarer to prevent her from getting hits out.
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]]: Octopus is here mainly to serve as a line of defense against incoming Brollow waves. Mainly helpful for the traditional lure strategies for this stage, but can be used fine enough for rushing strategies.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
Generally, any Uber that has above 9 speed or has some kind of [[Special Abilities|special ability]] against [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] or [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies should do well here.

*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: Balrog's gigantic DPS should never be underestimated, especially on a stage where the main boss has such a large blindspot. While you may need to time Balrog, if he gets into Queen B's blindspot his huge damage will obliterate any peon that dares to stand in his way, as well as get huge damage off on THE SLOTH. Even if he dies, his blazing fast recharge time allows you to just send another right after.
*[[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]]: Similar to Balrog, Cradle does have less burst damage potential, but has more health to compensate. Cradle's Waves extend its reach substantially, with any Brollow or Kroxo entering it melting immediately. While Cradle does have KB vs. Floating/Aliens, it's not very reliable and should just be seen as a nice bonus rather than the main appeal of bringing this Uber here.
*[[Count Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Vampiric Yukimura]]/[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]]: Both Yukimuras are speedy rushers that can easily get into Queen B's blindspot, serving as a huge source of free damage.
*[[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Thunder Jack]]: Thunder Jack destroys this stage. His good speed, huge healthpool, high DPS and 50% Knockback vs. Aliens means that he'll see value against any phase of this stage. Waves of Brollows can be continously repelled with his rapid attacks (though be wary of him dying), Queen B can be continously pushed back to the base, and his Multi-Hits will rack up very quickly against THE SLOTH.
*[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: Kai's good speed will allow her to sneak into Queen B's blindspot, and even if Slowed her massive health pool will allow her to act as an immobile line of defense for if you lose ground. Kai also has loads of damage as well as a good base health pool, meaning that she can stall not only the Brollows but also THE SLOTH and Kroxos and deal good damage to them in the process.
*[[Twinstars (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Twinstars Φ]]: Twinstars has good speed and a decent cooldown, but more importantly has insane burst potential in their rapid attacks and Massive vs. Aliens. They won't be of much use against THE SLOTH, but for getting damage knockbacks on Queen B Twinstars will perform well.
*[[Tekachi (Uber Rare Cat)|Tetsukachi]]: Similar to Kai, Tetsukachi is able to hold the line against the Brollows and Kroxos. While Tetsukachi has zero offensive value, having a stable line of defense is very valuable here.
*[[Strike Unit R.E.I. (Uber Rare Cat)|Strike Unit R.E.I.]]: Just like how [[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai]] easily counters the Red threats in [[Realm of Carnage (Deadly)|Realm of Carnage]], R.E.I. can demolish Queen B and the Brollows with huge damage against Floating as well as Slow Immunity. Try to prevent R.E.I. from getting hit from THE SLOTH, as her health isn't the greatest.
*[[Trixi the Merc (Uber Rare Cat)|Trixi the Revenant]]: Trixi is Slow Immune and targets everything aside from the Brollows. Her Freeze is also very powerful here, basically disabling Queen B and making timing much more lenient.
*[[Iz the Dancer (Uber Rare Cat)|Iz the Alluring Dancer]]: Iz is extremely good here, having a good Speed, high burst potential against the Traited enemies here, being disposable, and being Slow Immune. Similarly, [[Iz the Dancer of Grief (Uber Rare Cat)|Iz the Lady of Mourning]] has similar properties, but targets Traitless instead. Her damage against Traited isn't very notable, so try to clear out the Brollow/Kroxo waves before deploying her.
*[[Netherworld Nymph Lunacia (Uber Rare Cat)|Netherworld Nymph Lunacia]]: DLuna targets every single trait present in this stage, can Weaken Brollows and THE SLOTH, has very high base stats, and is Slow Immune, essentially guaranteeing you a free win.
*[[Squire Luno (Uber Rare Cat)|Squire Luno]]: Luno moves fast and attacks a bit fast, but more importantly has a broken Conjure that Knockbacks and creates a Mini-Surge, which forces anything in it to be pushed back. Given Luno's fast cooldown and move speed, you can constantly send out Luno to Knockback any enemies that might have moved forward due to your own human error.
*[[Blanka (Uber Rare Cat)|Blanka]]: Blanka has a fast cooldown, while his gigantic damage to Aliens and forward-piercing Omni-Strike will allow him to deal huge damage to Queen B.
*[[Saber (Uber Rare Cat)|Saber Alter CC]]: Similarly to Vampiric Yukimura, Saber is a fast anti-Floating rusher who has very high damage, allowing her to wipe a wave of Brollows as well as get some damage onto THE SLOTH thanks to her Long Distance.
*[[Lone Moon Lunos (Uber Rare Cat)|Lone Moon Lunos]]: Lunos targets all traits in this stage, allowing him to solo this stage with his conjure. Just make sure to use his conjure to get rid of the Brollows as well as making sure to spawn him alone, so he doesn't he caught in Queen B's slow.

